body:
If a graphic defines: 
```
"properties": {
      "name": {
        "type": "number",
        "title": "Countdown",
        "default": "10"
      }
    }
```

But I send:
`/renderers/{rendererId}/target/graphicInstance/load`
```
{
  "renderTarget": {
    "bank": 1,
    "layer": 14
  },
  "graphicId": "simple-l3rd",
  "params": {
    "data": {
      "Countdown": "10 Seconds"
    }
  }
}
```
Should the server respond with a 500? or a 550?

Should there be a response body specifically for type mismatches or would this be apart of the 550 response?
Does the spec say if this is a hard fail condition?

Based on: https://ograf.ebu.io/v1/specification/docs/Specification.html
and: https://ograf.ebu.io/v1/specification/open-api/docs/index.html

The graphics spec refers to editable fields of a graphic as `properties`

```
"properties": {
      "name": {
        "type": "string",
        "title": "Name",
        "default": "John Doe"
      }
    }
```

But the server spec shows what looks like populating these same fields using the terminology parameters/params:
```
  "params": {
    "data": {
      "name": "John Doe"
    }
  }
```

